IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.1 (R-Q7A/B/C, RULED 2026-09-07, BUILT
-- 2026-09-15): the ANCHORED deadline, `WITHIN d OF anchor`.
--
-- Unanchored, a WITHIN counts from where the language puts it: under HENCE,
-- the join's firing (§5.1); under LEST, today, the event that revealed the
-- miss (§5.2 owes the missed deadline). Anchored, it is ABSOLUTE — the
-- anchor's instant plus d — and the anchor is one of
--
--   OF THE JOIN        the instant the ENCLOSING obligation's join fired
--   OF THE DEADLINE    the enclosing obligation's deadline
--   OF THE ARMING      the instant the enclosing obligation was entered
--   OF e               an instant: a NUMBER on the trace's clock, or a DATE
--
-- where "enclosing" means the obligation whose HENCE or LEST this one is the
-- continuation of. Every trace below pins one anchor to a number, and the
-- number the breach reports is the deadline the anchor produced.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob


§ `OF THE JOIN is the HENCE default, said out loud`

-- The landlord's five days run from Alice's signature — exactly as they would
-- with no anchor at all (run-barrier.l4 pins the unanchored form to the same
-- arithmetic). A delivery at day 13 is timely; the breach at 14 reports the
-- deadline 8 + 5 = 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the join` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 13

#TRACE `of the join` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14


§ `OF THE DEADLINE under HENCE: the cure period runs from when performance fell due`

-- Alice signs early, at day 8, but the landlord's five days count from day
-- 30, when her signature fell due — not from day 8. Delivery at 35 is timely;
-- the breach at 36 reports 30 + 5 = 35.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 35

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 36


§ `OF THE DEADLINE under LEST: the cure period runs from the missed deadline`

-- Alice misses day 10. The miss is revealed by her late signature at day 14,
-- and today's UNANCHORED rule would start her cure period there (§5.2 records
-- that as the change still owed). Anchored, the cure period runs from the
-- deadline she missed: 10 + 5 = 15, whatever day the miss came to light. Her
-- signature at 14 is re-offered to the LEST and discharges it; a signature at
-- 16 does not, and the breach reports 15.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure from the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 14

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 16


§ `OF THE ARMING: within so many days of the agreement, two levels down`

-- Three obligations in a chain. The landlord delivers (armed at 0); then Bob
-- signs (armed at the delivery); then Alice signs WITHIN 40 OF THE ARMING.
-- THE ARMING is the arming of the ENCLOSING obligation — Bob's, which was
-- entered when the landlord delivered, at day 5 — so Alice's deadline is
-- 5 + 40 = 45, not 20 + 40 = 60 (her own arming) and not 0 + 40 (the
-- outermost rule's). The nearest enclosing obligation is the one an anchor
-- names.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of the arming` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 30
           HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 40 OF THE ARMING))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 45

#TRACE `of the arming` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 46

-- At the top level there is no enclosing obligation, and THE ARMING is the
-- obligation's own arming: the default, allowed and pointless. Armed at 3,
-- due 3 + 7 = 10.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`own arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 7 OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `own arming` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 11


§ `OF an instant: a NUMBER on the trace's clock, or a DATE`

closingDate MEANS 20

-- A NUMBER is an instant on the trace's own scale, whatever the obligation's
-- clock read when it was entered: armed at 3, due 20 + 5 = 25.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`of a number` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF closingDate

#TRACE `of a number` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 26

-- A DATE is lowered to its serial (DATE_SERIAL), so on a trace whose clock is
-- date serials it means the calendar date: WITHIN 0 OF 30 June 2026 is
-- "by 30 June". A signature on 1 July reports the deadline as the serial of
-- 30 June 2026.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`by thirty june` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 0 OF (YMD 2026 6 30)

#TRACE `by thirty june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 30))

#TRACE `by thirty june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1))

-- Already expired at arming: the contract begins on 1 July and the deadline
-- was five days after 20 June. That is not an error; the first event reveals
-- the expiry, and the breach reports the deadline that had already passed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`already expired` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 5 OF (YMD 2026 6 20)

#TRACE `already expired` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1)) WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 2))

-- The duration is any NUMBER expression; in the WITHIN slot OF is the anchor,
-- so an applied duration is bracketed (or written with juxtaposed arguments,
-- `twice 3`). Due 0 + 6 = 6.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER GIVETH A NUMBER DECIDE twice n IS n TIMES 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`applied duration` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN (twice OF 3) OF THE ARMING

#TRACE `applied duration` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 7


§ `Under a barrier`

-- THE DEADLINE in a barrier's HENCE is the ONCE line's WITHIN when one is
-- written — the deadline on the whole (R-T2) — and otherwise the act deadline
-- of the member whose completion fired the join. Here there is no ONCE-line
-- WITHIN: every member was due at 14, so the landlord's five days run from
-- 14, not from Bob's signature at 9. Delivery at 19 is timely; at 20 the
-- breach reports 14 + 5 = 19.
--
-- Under the barrier's LEST, THE DEADLINE is the deadline the failing member
-- missed: Bob's, at 14. The refund is due 14 + 5 = 19 whether the miss came
-- to light at day 15 or day 20.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund  (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 19

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

-- With a WITHIN on the ONCE line, THE DEADLINE in the HENCE is that one:
-- the group's deadline, 30, so delivery is due 30 + 5 = 35.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy, bounded as a whole` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `the tenancy, bounded as a whole` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 36

-- A join line's own WITHIN may be anchored too — to THE ARMING (the EVERY's
-- own arming, which is also what it counts from unanchored) or to an
-- instant; not to THE JOIN or THE DEADLINE, which it is what defines. Here
-- the EVERY is nested under the landlord's delivery, so it is armed at day 5,
-- and its members are due 5 + 14 = 19: Bob's signature at 20 breaches.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`after delivery` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
              MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
              ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 14 OF THE ARMING
              HENCE  FULFILLED
              LEST   BREACH)
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `after delivery` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 19

#TRACE `after delivery` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 5
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 6
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20

-- The whole group must have signed by instant 105 (100 + 5), whatever day
-- the EVERY was armed. That is the state deadline, and — as a join-line
-- WITHIN written alone always does (R-T2) — it also bounds each act, so it
-- is what the LEST's THE DEADLINE names: the refund is due 105 + 1 = 106.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`by instant 105` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 5 OF 100
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 1 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `by instant 105` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 105

#TRACE `by instant 105` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 106
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 107


§ `Under a fork`

-- Each member's HENCE is its own continuation, and THE DEADLINE in it is
-- that member's deadline. Both tenants were due at 14, so both deliveries
-- are due 14 + 2 = 16 — the one Alice's signature at 1 spawned no earlier
-- than the one Bob's at 9 did. A delivery at 17 breaches both; the compound
-- reports the first, and the deadline it reports is 16.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`receipts` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 17


§ `What a residual prints`

-- An obligation that has not met an event prints its deadline as written,
-- anchor and all. One that has prints the days remaining: the landlord's
-- deadline was fixed at 30 + 5 = 35 when Bob's (irrelevant) signature at day
-- 20 was scrutinised, and 15 days remain. The anchor was resolved once, at
-- that first event, and is spent.
#EVAL `of the join`

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8

#TRACE `of the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 20

-- An inline rule, so the natural-language linearisation of an anchor
-- ("within 7 of the arming") is in this file's .nlg golden too.
#EVAL PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 7 OF THE ARMING
